Berberine hydrochloride is an isolated alkaloid salt, so it falls in Chapter 29, heading 2939 (vegetable alkaloids, natural or reproduced by synthesis, and their salts, ethers, esters and other derivatives). Berberine is an isoquinoline alkaloid. Heading 2939 has subheadings for opium alkaloids, cinchona, caffeine, ephedrines, theophylline, lysergic acid, nicotine and others, and berberine is not named in any of them. It therefore goes in the "Other" subheading, 2939.99.

I recall CBP rulings that classify berberine hydrochloride in 2939.99.8100 or 2939.99.8000, but I am not certain of the exact statistical suffix. The 2939.99 subheading is split into 2939.99.10 (Other: alkaloids...) and 2939.99.80 (Other). I believe the later one, 2939.99.8100 "Other: Other" has been used, and 2939.99.8100 is the most likely.

{"hts_code": "2939.99.8100", "reason": "Berberine hydrochloride is an isolated, high-purity vegetable (isoquinoline) alkaloid salt, which falls under heading 2939 in the residual 'other' alkaloids subheading."}
